<title>UK: Sims sells beef unit to Ireland's Dawn.</title>
<headline>Sims sells beef unit to Ireland's Dawn.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>British food producer Sims Food Group Plc said on Monday it planned to sell its retail business for 12.15 million stg cash to Ireland's Dawn Holdings Ltd.</p>
<p>The retail division is mainly involved in the slaughtering, butchering and packaging of beef. Sims said it had sought the sell the unit because red meat consumption was in long-term decline.</p>
<p>Sims said in April that a plan for a management buy-out had been revived after it was suspended last year because of the &quot;mad cow&quot; crisis.</p>
<p>But it said it finally agreed terms with Dawn after talking to several interested parties.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
